course: dictionary
lesson: 14075
title: Mealtime and the words around it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A mealtime is a time of day when people eat a meal. Breakfast, lunch and dinner are all mealtimes. Mealtime is a noun, so it names a time, and it can also be plural: mealtimes.
explain: «We have no phones at mealtimes in our house.» The phrase at mealtimes means every time people sit down to eat, so the rule applies whenever the family is eating.
explain: «Family mealtime is our favourite part of the day.» Family tells you who is eating: the whole family, together. Look at the words around a new word to find its meaning.
fact: A mealtime is a time of day when people eat a meal.
fact: Breakfast, lunch and dinner are the main mealtimes of the day.
fact: «At mealtimes» means whenever people are eating a meal.
fact: «Family mealtime» means a meal eaten together by a family.
fact: Mealtimes can be fixed on a timetable, so they happen at the same time every day.
exercise: «We wash our hands before mealtimes.» What is a mealtime? | *A time of day when people eat a meal | A time of day when people go to sleep | A game played after school | A kind of plate
exercise: «There are no phones allowed at mealtimes in our house.» What does at mealtimes mean here? | During a football match | After the house is cleaned | Only on a Sunday afternoon | *Whenever people are eating a meal
exercise: Find and copy one word that names a mealtime. | blue | quickly | *breakfast | sleepy
test: «Family mealtime is when we all sit down together to eat.» What is family mealtime? | A film the family watches together | *A meal eaten together by a family | A long walk in the park | A school trip
test: Which of these is not a mealtime? | *Bedtime | Lunch | Dinner | Breakfast
exam: Mia says, «Mealtimes are fixed on our timetable, so we always eat at the same times.» What does fixed mean here? | *Set and never changing | Glued to the table | Very quick | Broken and needing repair
